---
import { productCopy } from './product-copy';
---
<section id="integrations" class="py-16 sm:py-24 px-6 border-t border-overlay/10">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl">
    <div class="grid lg:grid-cols-2 gap-8 lg:gap-20 mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-display-sm max-w-xl">Keep the agent you already use.</h2>
      <p class="text-lg text-ink-200 leading-relaxed">Use a compatible MCP client or build against the REST API. Your business knowledge, tone, and reply instructions stay with your agent.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-8">
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-overlay/15 p-6 sm:p-8">
        <h3 class="text-2xl mb-3">Connect through MCP</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-200 leading-relaxed">In Replaid, open Agents → Connections. Copy your MCP URL, add it to your client, and sign in to authorize your team.</p>
        <p class="text-sm text-ink-200 mt-4">Use OAuth where supported. Some clients need an agent token. Client features and account requirements vary.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-overlay/15 p-6 sm:p-8">
        <h3 class="text-2xl mb-3">Build with the API</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-200 leading-relaxed">Use a team agent token to read conversations and request actions through REST. Receive message events through signed webhooks.</p>
        <p class="text-sm text-ink-200 mt-4">MCP and REST use the same action policies and execution records.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-8 border-l-2 border-accent pl-6 max-w-4xl">
      <h3 class="text-lg mb-2">Want your agent to react to new messages?</h3>
      <p class="text-ink-200 leading-relaxed">{productCopy.automation}</p>
    </div>
    {Astro.url.pathname.replace(/\/$/, '') !== '/docs/connect-your-agent' && (
      <a href="/docs/connect-your-agent" class="inline-block mt-8 font-semibold underline underline-offset-4">Read the connection guide</a>
    )}
  </div>
</section>
